<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav March inflation 1.0 pct vs 0.6 pct in Feb.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav March inflation 1.0 pct vs 0.6 pct in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INFLATION	  MAR 97     FEB 97	MAR 96</p>
<p> monthly RPI index rise    + 1.0	+ 0.6	 + 7.2</p>
<p> yr/yr percent change	+26.4	+32.4	+126.7</p>
<p>NOTES -- March RPI was 17.7 percent up against the average in 1996.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-March RPI was 16.7 percent up against the average in 1996 and 32 percent up against the same three-month period last year.</p>
<p>Figures refer to Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 222 4305</p>
</text>
